{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-01T22:11:52.411Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\nI implemented the shared readers in the task's scope:\n\n- **`src/core/report/stream-reads.ts`** — added `readSharedFile` (shares one read per resolved path + parser in scope, rejects with the fs error, caches failures so they aren't retried), `readTextFile` (identity parser through `readSharedFile`), and `freezeDeep` (deep-freezes objects/arrays, skips already-frozen values). Extended the scope with a separate `shared` parser map.\n- **`src/core/report/change-reads.ts`** (new) — `readBriefData` and `readManifestObject`, each with one module-level parser, deep-freezing results and returning null on missing/unreadable/malformed input.\n- **`tests/report-shared-reads.test.ts`** (new) — 22 tests covering every acceptance line, counting reads via `mock.method` on `node:fs/promises`.\n\nBoth verifies pass: `node --import tsx --test tests/report-shared-reads.test.ts` (22/22) and `pnpm verify` (typechecks, build, full suite, lint). One early failure (`no-skipped-in-src.test.ts` flagged the word \"skipped\" in a comment) was fixed by rewording the comment."}}
